  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the primary uncertainty is whether the basic pipeline is sound and what performance level to expect. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable baseline in the design space: it uses a fast, well-understood encoder (PCA), the simplest profile setting, and a single modality. Running this first establishes a reference performance level against which all subsequent encoder, profile, modality, and fusion choices can be meaningfully compared. If it performs poorly, we immediately know the issue lies in representation or task difficulty before investing budget in complex multimodal or transformer-based configurations. If it performs reasonably, it confirms the pipeline and lets us efficiently test whether multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), or adding an image modality provide incremental gains. This maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget by anchoring the entire search to a clear baseline."
}

